```text name=README.md
# Synthetic Traffic Scripts

Contents:
- synthetic-transaction-playwright.js — headless browser synthetic transaction (Playwright)
- synthetic-transaction-k6.js — HTTP-level synthetic transaction (k6)

Important: Only run these against sites you own or have explicit permission to test.

## Quick local setup

Prerequisites:
- git installed
- Node.js (for Playwright)
- k6 (for load tests) or Docker

1) Playwright (local)

```bash
# create folder and install
mkdir synthetic && cd synthetic
npm init -y
npm install playwright
# install browsers and deps
npx playwright install --with-deps
# run
BASE_URL=https://your-site.com SEARCH_TERM="my query" node synthetic-transaction-playwright.js
```

2) k6 (local)

Install k6: https://k6.io/docs/getting-started/installation/

Run:

```bash
BASE_URL=https://your-site.com SEARCH_TERM="my query" k6 run synthetic-transaction-k6.js
```

## Scheduling

- Cron example (every 5 minutes) for Playwright:

```cron
*/5 * * * * cd /path/to/repo && BASE_URL=https://your-site.com /usr/bin/node synthetic-transaction-playwright.js >> /var/log/synthetic.log 2>&1
```

- Systemd unit/timer examples are included in the `systemd/` folder.

## Safety & Best Practices
- Never run high-volume k6 tests against production without ops approval.
- Use dedicated test accounts for authenticated journeys.
- Monitor target system metrics and abort tests if error rates rise.
```

```yaml name=.github/workflows/run-playwright.yml
name: Synthetic Playwright Transaction
on:
  schedule:
    # every 5 minutes
    - cron: '*/5 * * * *'
  workflow_dispatch:

jobs:
  run-playwright:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Setup Node
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '18'
      - name: Install dependencies
        run: npm ci || npm install
      - name: Run Playwright synthetic transaction
        env:
          BASE_URL: ${{ secrets.SYNTHETIC_BASE_URL }}
          SEARCH_TERM: 'monitor test'
        run: node synthetic-transaction-playwright.js || echo "Script exited with $?"
      - name: Upload screenshot artifact
        if: always()
        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: synthetic-screenshot
          path: synthetic-screenshot-*.png
```

```yaml name=.github/workflows/run-k6.yml
name: Synthetic k6 Transaction
on:
  schedule:
    - cron: '0 */1 * * *' # every hour
  workflow_dispatch:

jobs:
  run-k6:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Run k6 using Docker
        env:
          BASE_URL: ${{ secrets.SYNTHETIC_BASE_URL }}
        run: |
          docker run --rm -v "${{ github.workspace }}:/scripts" -w /scripts -e BASE_URL="${BASE_URL}" loadimpact/k6 run synthetic-transaction-k6.js || true
      - name: Upload raw k6 output (if produced)
        if: always()
        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: k6-output
          path: k6-summary-*.txt || synthetic-k6-results.txt || .
```

```ini name=systemd/system/synthetic-playwright.service
[Unit]
Description=Run synthetic Playwright transaction

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=/home/ubuntu/synthetic
Environment=BASE_URL=https://your-site.example
ExecStart=/usr/bin/node /home/ubuntu/synthetic/synthetic-transaction-playwright.js
```

```ini name=systemd/system/synthetic-playwright.timer
[Unit]
Description=Run synthetic Playwright every 5 minutes

[Timer]
OnBootSec=2min
OnUnitActiveSec=5min
Persistent=true

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
```

